  "answer": "This feature request has been filed several times before. The main ticket is PowerToys#21313, a utility to disable the keyboard (and mouse/touchscreen) while cleaning. PowerToys#33581 and PowerToys#20445 (\"Keyboard lock\") were closed as duplicates of it, and PowerToys#29382 (\"CleanKeys\") was closed as a duplicate of #20445. A maintainer said in #21313 that there are currently no plans to implement this in PowerToys. Please add a thumbs-up or your use case to #21313 instead of keeping a new ticket open. In the meantime, you can lock the PC with Win+L, put it to sleep, unplug or disconnect the keyboard, or use a third-party keyboard-lock or keyboard-cleaning tool."
